{"name":"Myth of the Plains","hex":"#8b6a4f","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"myth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional story which embodies a belief regarding some fact or phenomenon of experience, and in which often the forces of nature and of the soul are personified; a sacred narrative regarding a god, a hero, the origin of the world or of a people, etc.","Such stories as a genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/myth"},{"term":"plains","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of plain"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of plain"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plains"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myth","blocks":[{"text":"Myth is a genre of folklore consisting primarily of narratives that play a fundamental role in a society. For scholars, this is different from the ordinary sense of the term myth, meaning a belief that is not true, as the veracity of a piece of folklore is entirely irrelevant to determining whether it constitutes a myth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg/330px-Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myth","wikidata":"Q12827256"},{"title":"Plain","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, a plain, commonly known as flatland, is a flat expanse of land that generally has few rapid or steep changes in elevation. Natural vegetation in plains can include prairies/grasslands, forests, savanah, tundra, and desert biomes, among others. Plains occur as lowlands along valleys or at the base of mountains, as coastal plains, and as plateaus or uplands. Plains are one of the major landforms on earth, being present on all continents and covering more than one-third of the world's land area. Plains in many areas are important for agriculture. There are various types of plains, and biomes on them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Maniototoevening.jpg/330px-Maniototoevening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain","wikidata":"Q160091"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg/500px-Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg/1280px-Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg/500px-Hotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ballads of bravery (1877) part of Arthurian mythology","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHotherus_and_wood_maidens_by_Froelich.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/500px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/1280px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg/500px-Francesco_Hayez_028.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odysseus Overcome by Demodocus' Song, a mythological painting by Francesco Hayez, 1813–1815","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrancesco_Hayez_028.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Jesus-College-MS-111_00379_190r_%28cropped%29_Geraint